From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <dev@luneos.org>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:16:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] technology: add StartWPS and CancelWPS

com.webos.service.wifi/startwps, /createwpspin and /cancelwps drive WPS
at the technology level: the user pushes the button on the router and
ConnMan is expected to associate with whatever access point answers.
Upstream only supports the agent driven per-network form, where a target
service already exists and the agent returns a WPS field, so the adapter
had nothing to call.

Adds net.connman.Technology.StartWPS(pin) / CancelWPS() and the WPSFailed
signal, a start_wps/cancel_wps pair on connman_device_driver implemented
by the WiFi plugin, and the supplicant plumbing they need
(Interface.WPS.Cancel plus a wps_state callback so the plugin learns the
outcome).  On success the provisioned SSID is matched against the known
networks and handed to the normal association path.

Reworked from the webOS OSE ConnMan fork.  Note that the fork also
blocked service auto-connect for the duration of the WPS handshake via a
global flag in service.c; that is not carried over, so a known network
may be auto-connected while WPS is running, exactly as it can with
upstream's per-network WPS.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
